                        Movie Master v1.0
                        -----------------

Programming: Corey Badeaux

Movie Master was designed to store numbered and non-numbered tapes with
the movies on each tape. By numbering your video tape collection, you can
search thru the Video Tape Database by number, words, or partial words
found in the name of the movie. You can Add or Delete movies and if
you have to edit the file, just use the ALPHA-SORTER to fix any problems
with the text-based datafile and it will automatically sort up to
5000+ movies quickly in alphabetical order.

SEARCH MODE
-----------
Searh Movie Datafile by NUMBER, words, or partial words found in movie title.
Or leave entry blank to view all titles.

ADD MODE
--------
Add movie by entering number then title of movie. If you don't want a number
just leave entry blank. Once the title is entered, it will sort thru the data
file and place the new entry in it's alphabetical place in the file.

DELETE MODE
-----------
Searches for movies same way as in SEARCH MODE, but gives you the option
to delete the items found.

EDIT MODE
---------
Used the DOS EDIT command to edit the movie datafile, just in case you
have to.

ALPHA-SORTER
------------
Run this anytime you think your movies have gotten out of place.

